      "a": "Volcanic ash can cause scratches to the eyes and lungs because it is made of small particles that are hard and prickly [1]. It can also enter deep into the lungs with the air, causing increased coughing, shortness of breath, runny nose, and throat pain [2]. People with asthma or bronchitis may experience coughing fits, a feeling of tightness in the chest, and labored breathing, so they should be careful [2]. People with serious heart conditions should also be careful [2]. If volcanic ash gets into your eyes, wash it away with water instead of rubbing it with your hands. Remove contact lenses and wear glasses [2].",
